Headless option (AuroraConfig::headless, off by default)

For test runs on a desktop someone is using: the window is created hidden and never shown, a hidden
or unfocused window does not pause the frame loop (is_paused), and SDL_HINT_MAC_BACKGROUND_APP is set
before the video subsystem starts, so on macOS the process gets no Dock icon and is never activated.
Frames still render and present to the hidden window's surface.

--- a/include/aurora/aurora.h
+++ b/include/aurora/aurora.h
@@ -123,6 +123,14 @@
    * shows every draw, as on the console, at the cost of a stall the first time a pipeline is used.
    */
   bool blockingPipelines;
+
+  /*
+   * Headless (Seaborne patch 0022): the window is created hidden and never shown, a hidden or
+   * unfocused window does not pause the frame loop, and on macOS the process runs as a background
+   * application (SDL_HINT_MAC_BACKGROUND_APP: no Dock icon, never activated). Frames still render and
+   * present to the hidden window's surface, so EFB readbacks (screenshots) work as usual.
+   */
+  bool headless;
 } AuroraConfig;
 
 typedef struct {
